includes: Pro-level push from the 5-domain repo audit. NAVIGATION: the Arrange · Clips · Compose switcher is now a PERSISTENT bottom bar — always on screen (icon over label, selected = accent), so you can move between the timeline and the instrument from anywhere. All surfaces stay mounted, so switching never interrupts the Compose audio. The Compose Tools are no longer a flat scroll where chips hid off the side — they are now a STRUCTURED, COLLAPSIBLE panel: a "Tools" header with a chevron folds/unfolds the whole set, grouped by purpose (Editors · Audio & Bio · Connect · Visual & Learn) so every tool is visible at a glance. PIANO-ROLL PRECISION: notes are now timed in PPQ ticks (480 PPQ → 120 ticks/step), the keystone for unquantized capture, nudge and swing — notes can sit OFF the 16th grid and export sample-tight. The step view is unchanged, and old clips still load (legacy fallback). AUTOMATION FOUNDATION: an AutomationLane data model (tick-keyframed, hold/linear, normalized) — the tested base for Ableton-style parameter automation (UI + playback wiring next). SOUND — FELT SUB: the sub-bass now plays at a felt level by default (still silent at launch until you play), with missing-fundamental synthesis (2nd+3rd harmonics) so the bass reads at full pitch on phone/laptop speakers yet is felt in full on a sub/haptics. SOUND — VISUAL TRACKS THE ENVELOPE: the spectral-donut immersive visual now swells on attack and fades on the decay/reverb tail, breathing with the actual sound instead of the note grid. All changes are Xcode-Compile-Check green on every commit; AutomationLane + PPQ Note are unit-tested. Still honestly held for device A/B: brighter default tone + unison/detune richness (signature-sound choices), per-track FX, multi-track arrangement, club light/video.
